/* book Worked example 2: Q: A four-cylinder CI engine has a bore of 10 cm, a stroke of 12 cm and a compression ratio of 19. Find the clearance volume of one cylinder.
   1. Swept volume of one cylinder: Vs = 0.7854 × 10² × 12 = 942.5 cm³.
   2. From r = 1 + Vs/Vc: Vc = Vs/(r − 1) = 942.5/18.
   3. Vc = 52.4 cm³. The number of cylinders does not enter, because bore, stroke and r are all per cylinder.
   Answer: Vc = 52.4 cm³ per cylinder. */
