/* book exam traps: A CI engine compresses air only. Writing that it compresses a fuel-air mixture is the commonest error. | The injector and the spark plug are not interchangeable: one creates the mixture in hot air, the other lights a mixture already made. | A higher compression ratio is not always better: in SI it brings knock, in CI it brings higher peak pressure, heavier parts and more NOx. | Quantity control belongs to SI (throttle), quality control to CI (fuel quantity). Swapping the two words is a classic slip. | Octane measures resistance to self-ignition and cetane measures readiness to self-ignite. A good petrol is a poor diesel fuel and the other way round. */
